<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Selim I</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Selim I was Ottoman sultan from 1512 to 1520. He defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavids</a> at Chaldiran in 1514 and conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a> in 1516–1517, bringing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and the holy cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> under Ottoman rule. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a> and Mamluk Sultanate profiles note that his conquest ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> state and the shadow Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/selim-i.jpg" alt="Selim I" width="253" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Naḳḳāş ʿOs̠mān · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nakka%C5%9F_Selim.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
